WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.761 --> 00:00:13.971
I love this park.

2
00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:17.641
You can hide and feel safe.

3
00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.685
Maybe that's why I came here.

4
00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.688
To find myself.

5
00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.441
The night sky.
so dense and clear

6
00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.569
you could stick your hand in
and feel the stars.

7
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.488
Nature doesn't judge.
It's not bad or good.

8
00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:33.032
It just is.

9
00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.744
Sheila wasn't so lucky.

10
00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:39.079
Someone else found her first.

11
00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.897
Uh...

12
00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:06.857
Anna Pigeon.
Hello.

13
00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:10.069
Anna. it's Geoff.

14
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.906
- Geoff. it's dark out.
- I know.

15
00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.950
- It's early.
Why are you at work?

16
00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:19.036
Sheila Drury didn't
come back last night.

17
00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:20.120
What?

18
00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:21.914
Her mom called me.

19
00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.540
She's usually up by now.
They do the. uh...

20
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:25.000
- Wordle together.
- Yeah.

21
00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:27.044
Yeah.

22
00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:30.089
Damn. Sheila's always on time.

23
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.715
Okay. uh. I'm up.

24
00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:33.008
I'm heading out.

25
00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:34.093
Hey. wait 'til it's light.

26
00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.803
I got another call coming.

27
00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:37.389
- Who calls you at 6:00 AM?
- My sister.

28
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.474
Hey.

29
00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:43.018
How's New York?

30
00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:44.853
I know I've said this
to you before.

31
00:01:44.854 --> 00:01:47.189
but I'm worried about you.

32
00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.692
Molly. I gotta go look
for a missing park ranger.

33
00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:51.735
my friend. who's probably
stuck in a crevasse

34
00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:53.112
with her leg under a rock.

35
00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.114
So don't shrink me right now.

36
00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.699
It's Zach's birthday coming up.

37
00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.242
- Yeah. I know.
I was married to him.

38
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:00.953
I literally never forget.

39
00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.204
How are you gonna
get through this week?

40
00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:03.664
You know.

41
00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:05.165
Work and wine.

42
00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:06.917
Besides. I'm leaving
in two weeks.

43
00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:08.502
An astute psychiatrist would say

44
00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:10.504
that you're avoiding
your feelings.

45
00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:12.840
Oh. are you astute now?

46
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.094
Molly. coffee's done.

47
00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.679
I gotta go.

48
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.764
I love you.
- Stay safe.

49
00:02:20.765 --> 00:02:23.183
Don't die. or I will kill you.

50
00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:40.784
That's littering. friend.

51
00:02:40.785 --> 00:02:42.787
It'll biodegrade.

52
00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.665
Okay. first. it takes two years

53
00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.958
for a banana peel to decompose.

54
00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:49.626
so don't even try that angle.

55
00:02:49.627 --> 00:02:51.920
Second. I'm not just
a park ranger.

56
00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:54.631
I'm a law enforcement ranger.
so in this park I'm a cop.

57
00:02:54.632 --> 00:02:58.010
And third.
I'm feeling crabby today.

58
00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.971
So pick it up.

59
00:03:02.807 --> 00:03:05.768
See? Take only memories.
leave only footprints.

60
00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:06.894
Easy. right?

61
00:03:22.243 --> 00:03:24.537
Sheila!

62
00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.889
Sheila!

63
00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.703
Sh...

64
00:04:05.704 --> 00:04:07.914
Vultures.

65
00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.135
Ah! Ah!

66
00:04:21.136 --> 00:04:22.886
Ow...

67
00:04:22.887 --> 00:04:25.932
Okay. devil's claw.
you thorny SOB.

68
00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:28.852
We doin' this?

69
00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.782
No...

70
00:04:46.077 --> 00:04:47.787
No!

71
00:04:49.914 --> 00:04:51.750
Sh...

72
00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:57.296
I'm so sorry.

73
00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:08.224
Hey. Geoff. um...

74
00:05:09.684 --> 00:05:12.061
I found Sheila.

75
00:05:12.062 --> 00:05:14.021
She's dead.
- Sh...

76
00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:16.190
Something feels off.

77
00:05:16.191 --> 00:05:18.192
- Anna. there's a...
there's a storm warning.

78
00:05:18.193 --> 00:05:20.444
I'll send the team later.
Come back.

79
00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:22.237
For your own safety. all right?

80
00:05:22.238 --> 00:05:24.114
I'm not leaving her
to the vultures. Geoff.

81
00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.035
Anna.

82
00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:30.412
- Sorry. uh. signal's bad.
I can't hear you.

83
00:05:30.413 --> 00:05:32.916
Oh. man. this park's the worst.

84
00:05:38.254 --> 00:05:39.923
Deep wounds.

85
00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.843
No scratches.

86
00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:48.306
Belly's intact.
That's weird.

87
00:05:49.724 --> 00:05:51.141
And no bite marks.

88
00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:10.828
Go.

89
00:06:10.829 --> 00:06:13.080
Go!

90
00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.364
- Is it bad?
Anna say it was bad?

91
00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:48.991
Yeah.

92
00:06:48.992 --> 00:06:49.825
Since you're
a law enforcement ranger.

93
00:06:49.826 --> 00:06:51.076
you gotta toughen up.

94
00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.870
I am tough.

95
00:06:52.871 --> 00:06:55.039
I come from a family
of park rangers and cops.

96
00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.082
And Manny's been in the army.

97
00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.043
I think we're pretty tough.

98
00:06:59.044 --> 00:07:01.795
- More resilient than tough.
- Yeah. yeah. yeah.

99
00:07:01.796 --> 00:07:03.797
Come on. we got work to do.

100
00:07:03.798 --> 00:07:05.842
Let's bring Sheila home.

101
00:07:07.802 --> 00:07:09.803
Anna.

102
00:07:09.804 --> 00:07:11.096
Anna?

103
00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.932
Over here.

104
00:07:20.482 --> 00:07:23.025
Oh...

105
00:07:23.026 --> 00:07:26.320
Yeah.

106
00:07:26.321 --> 00:07:28.447
Looks like a mountain lion kill.

107
00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.282
Doesn't have the hallmarks.

108
00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.284
Cats eat what they kill.

109
00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:33.619
If the cat dragged her in here.

110
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.245
her guts would be everywhere.

111
00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:36.872
She'd have cuts from
the devil's claw.

112
00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:38.415
I know I'm not law enforcement.

113
00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:40.834
just humble paths and roadways.

114
00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:43.170
But Sheila was
on a transect. right?

115
00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:46.423
- Yeah. tracking cats.
- She tracked them too well.

116
00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:48.926
Okay. what if the cat
dragged her here.

117
00:07:48.927 --> 00:07:51.136
going backwards?

118
00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:52.971
The cat would have
sustained a cut.

119
00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.431
Cat didn't have any cuts on it.

120
00:07:54.432 --> 00:07:57.142
You saw it?

121
00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:59.937
- Lived to tell the tale.
- What's it doing here then?

122
00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:02.314
It was hunting that raccoon.

123
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:04.275
Living its life.

124
00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:08.862
So what killed her then.
if not the cat?

125
00:08:08.863 --> 00:08:10.907
People.

126
00:08:15.078 --> 00:08:16.955
Come on. you guys. help me
get her into the stokes.

127
00:08:20.875 --> 00:08:22.419
Careful.

128
00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:31.010
Here.

129
00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:54.575
One. two. three.

130
00:09:29.611 --> 00:09:31.571
Don't do it.

131
00:09:36.618 --> 00:09:38.285
You can still try
and rob this gas station.

132
00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:40.371
or you can slide that gun
over to me

133
00:09:40.372 --> 00:09:42.122
and you can go in there
and get me some Twizzlers.

134
00:09:42.123 --> 00:09:44.584
It's up to you.

135
00:09:46.127 --> 00:09:48.087
Hey.
- Hey. Frederick.

136
00:09:48.088 --> 00:09:50.464
It's Anna Pigeon Pigeon!

137
00:09:50.465 --> 00:09:53.550
Hey. it's been a while.
Thought you'd flown the coop.

138
00:09:53.551 --> 00:09:55.969
Uh. hey. I need your help.

139
00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.596
You busy?
- No.

140
00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:58.514
Hold on.

141
00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.021
Yeah. where you at?

142
00:10:21.079 --> 00:10:23.956
Did you find my daughter?

143
00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.418
Kelli. I have some bad news.

144
00:10:46.104 --> 00:10:47.605
What the hell?

145
00:10:49.024 --> 00:10:50.399
Harlan! Is that
dead goat in a cage

146
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.609
because you're hunting the cat?

147
00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.571
- Trapping the cat.
Geoff authorized it.

148
00:10:56.239 --> 00:10:58.490
Sorry. Anna.

149
00:10:58.491 --> 00:11:01.118
Thanks for lending us
your guys. Jerry D.

150
00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:03.037
This is bullsh...

151
00:11:03.038 --> 00:11:05.122
- Who is that?
- Anna.

152
00:11:05.123 --> 00:11:06.790
Law enforcement gal.

153
00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:08.626
So that's Anna Pigeon.

154
00:11:12.213 --> 00:11:13.172
Geoff's in a meeting.

155
00:11:13.173 --> 00:11:14.882
Anna!

156
00:11:14.883 --> 00:11:16.633
You're using ranch hands
to trap that cat?

157
00:11:16.634 --> 00:11:18.093
It killed Sheila.

158
00:11:18.094 --> 00:11:19.303
Are we not gonna
investigate that?

159
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:21.513
Why do you want to
overcomplicate this?

160
00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:23.599
Cat didn't do it. Geoff.

161
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.476
Nobody's ever been
killed by a cougar

162
00:11:25.477 --> 00:11:28.062
in Glacier National Park.
in all of time.

163
00:11:28.063 --> 00:11:29.813
In all of Glacier!

164
00:11:29.814 --> 00:11:31.398
Well. there's a first
for everything.

165
00:11:31.399 --> 00:11:33.651
If you trap and move
that cat. she will die.

166
00:11:33.652 --> 00:11:35.402
That's what happens.

167
00:11:35.403 --> 00:11:37.613
Cougars in the new territory
will kill her.

168
00:11:37.614 --> 00:11:39.239
This time of year
she'll have cubs. too.

169
00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.783
Her cubs will die.

170
00:11:40.784 --> 00:11:43.786
Anna. you went over my head.

171
00:11:43.787 --> 00:11:46.372
Special Agent Stanton
drove all the way here

172
00:11:46.373 --> 00:11:48.707
for a cat kill?

173
00:11:48.708 --> 00:11:50.751
Yeah. we know each other.

174
00:11:50.752 --> 00:11:51.835
My first year on the job.
somebody tried to kill me.

175
00:11:51.836 --> 00:11:53.504
He...
- I investigated.

176
00:11:53.505 --> 00:11:56.048
Oh. well. that
explains everything.

177
00:11:56.049 --> 00:11:58.467
Lack of eviscerations.
no cuts from the devil's claw.

178
00:11:58.468 --> 00:12:00.761
I wanted a second opinion.
Geoff. which I don't regret.

179
00:12:00.762 --> 00:12:03.515
Eh! Agent Stanton.
what's your view?

180
00:12:05.683 --> 00:12:07.267
I know this is emotional
for you. Anna.

181
00:12:07.268 --> 00:12:10.479
but you don't have
much to go on.

182
00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.398
Are you serious?

183
00:12:12.399 --> 00:12:14.401
Anything else?

184
00:12:16.361 --> 00:12:19.072
Sorry she wasted your time.

185
00:12:36.256 --> 00:12:38.508
- Want another one?
- Yeah.

186
00:12:41.803 --> 00:12:43.846
Saint Kateri.

187
00:12:43.847 --> 00:12:46.182
The patron saint
of the environment.

188
00:12:51.813 --> 00:12:54.065
I heard about the dead ranger.

189
00:12:55.442 --> 00:12:57.235
For a minute. I...

190
00:12:58.737 --> 00:13:00.697
For a minute I thought
it was you.

191
00:13:46.951 --> 00:13:49.412
Oh. my God.

192
00:13:51.289 --> 00:13:53.249
Sheila's backpack.

193
00:13:56.753 --> 00:13:59.463
Rain jacket.

194
00:13:59.464 --> 00:14:03.884
First aid.

195
00:14:03.885 --> 00:14:05.677
Phone.

196
00:14:11.518 --> 00:14:12.518
Water.

197
00:14:12.519 --> 00:14:14.228
Water?

198
00:14:14.229 --> 00:14:16.397
Sheila wasn't
carrying any water.

199
00:14:16.398 --> 00:14:18.524
Why would
an experienced park ranger

200
00:14:18.525 --> 00:14:21.360
head into the back country
without water?

201
00:14:21.361 --> 00:14:22.486
She wouldn't.

202
00:14:22.487 --> 00:14:22.529
Someone took her there.

203
00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:35.708
Hi.

204
00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:37.710
- Hey.
- You're here.

205
00:14:37.711 --> 00:14:40.754
Well. you called me. remember?

206
00:14:40.755 --> 00:14:42.632
Yeah. um...

207
00:14:47.887 --> 00:14:50.013
Right. right.

208
00:14:50.014 --> 00:14:52.017
Yep. just give...
Yep. I'll be right back.

209
00:14:54.602 --> 00:14:55.936
Why are you still
living like this?

210
00:14:55.937 --> 00:14:58.272
- Like what?
- Like a student?

211
00:14:58.273 --> 00:15:00.065
Or an old-timey drifter?

212
00:15:00.066 --> 00:15:02.026
I don't live like a drifter.

213
00:15:02.027 --> 00:15:03.360
You might as well ride
the rails and steal a pie.

214
00:15:03.361 --> 00:15:05.487
I mean. it made sense
when I first met you.

215
00:15:05.488 --> 00:15:06.697
But I read your employment file.

216
00:15:06.698 --> 00:15:08.741
You're excellent at your job.

217
00:15:08.742 --> 00:15:10.993
But you worked at five parks
in the last three years.

218
00:15:10.994 --> 00:15:12.828
and now you're
changing parks again.

219
00:15:12.829 --> 00:15:14.163
I like new places.

220
00:15:14.164 --> 00:15:15.831
I don't like office politics.

221
00:15:15.832 --> 00:15:17.750
- Really?
- Uh-huh.

222
00:15:17.751 --> 00:15:19.543
You have a fancy arts degree.

223
00:15:19.544 --> 00:15:21.336
parents back east.

224
00:15:21.337 --> 00:15:24.006
a sister who was
a big New York psychiatrist.

225
00:15:24.007 --> 00:15:26.592
And you're good. living in
old moldy ranger houses.

226
00:15:26.593 --> 00:15:28.719
going from park to park to park?

227
00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.804
You got all that from
my employment file?

228
00:15:30.805 --> 00:15:32.139
See. if I were profiling you.

229
00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.640
I'd think you were on the run.

230
00:15:33.641 --> 00:15:35.477
How's your divorce going?

231
00:15:37.812 --> 00:15:38.937
That's the campground
where they're putting in

232
00:15:38.938 --> 00:15:40.022
the RV hookups.

233
00:15:40.023 --> 00:15:41.231
That was Sheila's project.

234
00:15:43.234 --> 00:15:44.985
Some people don't want
drive-through nature.

235
00:15:44.986 --> 00:15:46.862
Better than people who
don't want nature at all.

236
00:15:51.785 --> 00:15:53.160
Sheila lived around the corner.

237
00:15:53.161 --> 00:15:54.663
The Pine Ridge ranger housing.

238
00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:03.796
Okay. there's no sign
of a struggle.

239
00:16:03.797 --> 00:16:05.590
Maybe it was someone she knew.

240
00:16:07.258 --> 00:16:08.801
- Okay. you're Sheila.
- That's interesting.

241
00:16:08.802 --> 00:16:10.260
I show up all friendly.

242
00:16:10.261 --> 00:16:12.596
tell you that we're
going on a hike.

243
00:16:12.597 --> 00:16:14.723
You pack her pack...

244
00:16:14.724 --> 00:16:15.599
If Sheila packed her pack.
she would have remembered

245
00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.935
to pack water.
- Okay. so I pack it.

246
00:16:17.936 --> 00:16:19.854
You comin' with me?
- No.

247
00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:24.192
Okay. we're missing something.

248
00:16:29.572 --> 00:16:31.949
Ah. sh...

249
00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.118
You okay?

250
00:16:34.119 --> 00:16:35.912
There's a cat under there.

251
00:16:38.206 --> 00:16:40.165
Let me try.

252
00:16:40.166 --> 00:16:41.667
Hey.

253
00:16:41.668 --> 00:16:43.877
Hi. come here.

254
00:16:43.878 --> 00:16:46.630
Hey. hi!
Hi.

255
00:16:46.631 --> 00:16:50.175
Hello. okay.
Soft power.

256
00:16:50.176 --> 00:16:51.719
Hard claws.

257
00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:52.761
Anna. it's Zoey.

258
00:16:52.762 --> 00:16:54.304
Hi.

259
00:16:54.305 --> 00:16:55.806
I got something
that you should see.

260
00:16:55.807 --> 00:16:57.725
Yeah. I'm coming.

261
00:16:57.726 --> 00:16:58.851
Do you mind giving me
a lift to the morgue?

262
00:16:58.852 --> 00:17:01.103
Unless you want to
sit in on the autopsy.

263
00:17:01.104 --> 00:17:02.479
- I'm good.
In a perfect world.

264
00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.189
the dead would be left in peace.

265
00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.817
Here.
Come here. buddy.

266
00:17:06.818 --> 00:17:08.694
Yeah. I'm gonna take him
to the office.

267
00:17:08.695 --> 00:17:10.863
Sheila's mom probably wants him.

268
00:17:10.864 --> 00:17:12.281
Hey. Piedmont.

269
00:17:17.037 --> 00:17:18.621
Hey.

270
00:17:20.123 --> 00:17:21.915
Parking permit's expired

271
00:17:21.916 --> 00:17:24.918
and the van belongs
to a Cory Nelson.

272
00:17:24.919 --> 00:17:27.713
I talked to this guy.

273
00:17:27.714 --> 00:17:29.048
Is that blood?

274
00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:30.675
Looks like it.

275
00:17:34.596 --> 00:17:36.305
All the doors are locked.

276
00:17:36.306 --> 00:17:38.766
Want me to get a lockout kit?

277
00:17:38.767 --> 00:17:40.184
The clock's ticking on that cat

278
00:17:40.185 --> 00:17:42.853
and on finding Sheila's killer.

279
00:17:42.854 --> 00:17:45.482
I don't think we have
time to spare. do you?

280
00:17:48.777 --> 00:17:51.987
All right. stand back
a little bit.

281
00:18:03.625 --> 00:18:05.250
Whoa.

282
00:18:05.251 --> 00:18:08.462
- This is creepy.
- As hell. man.

283
00:18:08.463 --> 00:18:10.673
More blood.

284
00:18:13.218 --> 00:18:15.010
Sheila's water bottle.

285
00:18:15.011 --> 00:18:16.971
- I saw him litter.
I should've known.

286
00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.855
Sheila's mom doesn't want it.

287
00:18:26.856 --> 00:18:28.732
Too painful. and I'm allergic.

288
00:18:28.733 --> 00:18:30.234
I can't take it.

289
00:18:30.235 --> 00:18:31.527
Kitty-kitty cat.

290
00:18:31.528 --> 00:18:34.697
Ooh. hell no!

291
00:18:34.698 --> 00:18:36.073
I got my rescue birds.
I can't.

292
00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.910
Anna. I know you're leaving.

293
00:18:39.911 --> 00:18:42.705
- I travel solo.
- Except me.

294
00:18:42.706 --> 00:18:44.999
I'm her mentee.

295
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.500
I named one of my crows
after you.

296
00:18:46.501 --> 00:18:48.127
So now you gotta stay.

297
00:18:48.128 --> 00:18:50.129
Hey. listen up.

298
00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:52.047
Ready! Huddle in.

299
00:18:52.048 --> 00:18:53.841
Cory Nelson.

300
00:18:53.842 --> 00:18:56.260
Posted some heated stuff
about new RV hookups.

301
00:18:56.261 --> 00:18:58.804
Sheila wrote him up for
being on a closed trail.

302
00:18:58.805 --> 00:19:00.431
He sent her death threats.

303
00:19:02.225 --> 00:19:04.143
All right. this is a manhunt.

304
00:19:04.144 --> 00:19:05.436
Sorry.

305
00:19:05.437 --> 00:19:07.439
Be safe.

306
00:19:10.483 --> 00:19:13.444
You're not really
leaving us. City girl?

307
00:19:13.445 --> 00:19:15.988
I put in a transfer to Badlands.

308
00:19:15.989 --> 00:19:18.282
End of the month.
- Ah.

309
00:19:18.283 --> 00:19:20.117
I get it.

310
00:19:20.118 --> 00:19:23.287
I've always been restless too.

311
00:19:23.288 --> 00:19:26.790
Spent some time fighting
in wars overseas.

312
00:19:26.791 --> 00:19:29.877
Ran hunting expeditions
in Alaska.

313
00:19:29.878 --> 00:19:31.880
Wrassled gators in Pensacola.

314
00:19:34.132 --> 00:19:38.552
I was a stage manager
in New York.

315
00:19:38.553 --> 00:19:39.970
Theater.

316
00:19:39.971 --> 00:19:42.806
Well. Miss Pigeon.

317
00:19:42.807 --> 00:19:44.933
It was a lifetime ago.

318
00:19:44.934 --> 00:19:48.062
- Adapt or die.
We live by our wits.

319
00:19:48.063 --> 00:19:50.481
You have to. given that
we're paid in sunsets.

320
00:19:50.482 --> 00:19:52.941
- Shh.
- Well. that's true.

321
00:19:52.942 --> 00:19:54.444
Shh.

322
00:19:56.029 --> 00:19:57.863
They said Cory had a red tent.

323
00:20:07.457 --> 00:20:09.917
Cory?

324
00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:12.169
Cory Nelson?

325
00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.171
I'm a law enforcement ranger.

326
00:20:14.172 --> 00:20:15.631
If you're in there.
I need you to put

327
00:20:15.632 --> 00:20:17.883
your hands outside
on the ground.

328
00:20:28.186 --> 00:20:38.947
These bites are all
from diving beetles.

329
00:20:49.165 --> 00:20:51.875
They're carnivorous.

330
00:20:51.876 --> 00:20:54.545
He had a hose and buckets
in his van.

331
00:20:54.546 --> 00:20:56.714
He must have been
collecting aquatic bugs.

332
00:20:56.715 --> 00:20:58.425
Interesting.

333
00:20:59.467 --> 00:21:02.177
They ate him after he died.

334
00:21:02.178 --> 00:21:03.679
Wait. then how did he die?

335
00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:06.223
He OD'd.

336
00:21:06.224 --> 00:21:08.184
You can see the needle mark.

337
00:21:20.613 --> 00:21:23.657
Cory OD'd on ketamine.

338
00:21:23.658 --> 00:21:26.702
He had a massive dose
in his system.

339
00:21:26.703 --> 00:21:30.247
- Fills that void.
Some people drink.

340
00:21:30.248 --> 00:21:33.167
Okay. I'm gonna ignore that.

341
00:21:33.168 --> 00:21:34.668
There was a syringe in his tent.

342
00:21:34.669 --> 00:21:36.754
but nothing to tie
his arm off with.

343
00:21:36.755 --> 00:21:38.590
He killed Sheila
and then he OD'd.

344
00:21:40.383 --> 00:21:41.759
Were there prints in
the tarp from the van?

345
00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.218
No prints.

346
00:21:43.219 --> 00:21:44.219
What about
Sheila's water bottle?

347
00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:45.596
Nope. he wiped them down.

348
00:21:45.597 --> 00:21:46.847
But why do that?

349
00:21:46.848 --> 00:21:48.515
Why wipe the prints off it

350
00:21:48.516 --> 00:21:50.309
and then leave it
in his own van?

351
00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:52.728
Also. where's Sheila's autopsy?

352
00:21:52.729 --> 00:21:54.271
Is that it?

353
00:21:54.272 --> 00:21:55.940
Look at this.

354
00:21:57.609 --> 00:21:58.734
Yeah. the puncture wounds
on her neck

355
00:21:58.735 --> 00:22:00.444
are three inches long.

356
00:22:00.445 --> 00:22:02.446
Right. saber tooth tigers
are extinct.

357
00:22:02.447 --> 00:22:03.906
Okay. okay. the wounds are deep.

358
00:22:03.907 --> 00:22:05.866
but that's not a theory.

359
00:22:05.867 --> 00:22:10.204
What if... someone
made it look like

360
00:22:10.205 --> 00:22:12.664
Sheila was killed by a cat.

361
00:22:12.665 --> 00:22:15.834
and when that didn't work.
they framed Cory for it?

362
00:22:15.835 --> 00:22:17.461
We need more to go on.

363
00:22:17.462 --> 00:22:18.629
All right. put somebody
at the scene.

364
00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:20.339
I don't know.

365
00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:22.425
I got meth labs
and a militia shooting.

366
00:22:24.636 --> 00:22:26.304
Good luck.

367
00:22:29.682 --> 00:22:31.725
Sorry about your friend.

368
00:22:31.726 --> 00:22:33.520
Thanks.

369
00:22:39.776 --> 00:22:41.610
What play are you seeing?

370
00:22:41.611 --> 00:22:43.696
It's a one man Hamlet.

371
00:22:43.697 --> 00:22:47.449
Worse comes to worst.
I think my thoughts.

372
00:22:47.450 --> 00:22:49.660
Zach played Hamlet.

373
00:22:49.661 --> 00:22:51.370
I know. honey.

374
00:22:51.371 --> 00:22:53.330
How's work and wine going?

375
00:22:53.331 --> 00:22:54.665
Drinking beer and doing laundry.

376
00:22:54.666 --> 00:22:56.834
which I find oddly soothing.

377
00:22:56.835 --> 00:22:58.836
That is truly sad.

378
00:22:58.837 --> 00:23:00.295
Why do people murder people?

379
00:23:00.296 --> 00:23:01.839
Is this theoretical

380
00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:02.756
or about your friend
who went missing?

381
00:23:02.757 --> 00:23:04.883
The latter.

382
00:23:04.884 --> 00:23:06.218
Well. it doesn't take
a med degree and five years

383
00:23:06.219 --> 00:23:08.387
of psychiatric residency
to figure that out.

384
00:23:08.388 --> 00:23:10.097
Four Ls.

385
00:23:10.098 --> 00:23:12.766
Love. Lust. Lucre aka money.
and Loathing.

386
00:23:12.767 --> 00:23:13.892
Well. there's no lucre here.

387
00:23:13.893 --> 00:23:15.728
Not a lot of loathing.

388
00:23:15.729 --> 00:23:17.730
Hey!

389
00:23:17.731 --> 00:23:19.898
I'm at the theater.

390
00:23:19.899 --> 00:23:22.860
Take a break from worrying.
I'll call you tomorrow.

391
00:23:22.861 --> 00:23:25.279
All right. got it.

392
00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:27.364
Good night. sweet princess.

393
00:23:27.365 --> 00:23:28.532
You know that's from
the end of Hamlet.

394
00:23:28.533 --> 00:23:29.616
where everyone's dead. right?

395
00:23:29.617 --> 00:23:31.577
Including Hamlet.
Spoiler.

396
00:23:31.578 --> 00:23:33.328
You know. you don't have
to solve every murder.

397
00:23:33.329 --> 00:23:35.122
'Night.

398
00:23:35.123 --> 00:23:36.416
Molly. can you just...

399
00:24:25.048 --> 00:24:27.758
Hey. you.

400
00:24:27.759 --> 00:24:29.802
You would've hated it here.

401
00:24:35.892 --> 00:24:37.727
I miss you.

402
00:24:42.691 --> 00:24:44.483
Happy birthday.

403
00:25:20.854 --> 00:25:22.146
Just got a call that
they're hitting golf balls

404
00:25:22.147 --> 00:25:24.690
up on Gunsight Ridge.

405
00:25:24.691 --> 00:25:26.483
What's wrong?

406
00:25:26.484 --> 00:25:28.694
Someone left a dead pigeon
on my doorstep.

407
00:25:28.695 --> 00:25:31.905
Well. Anna. you do have
a lot of admirers.

408
00:25:31.906 --> 00:25:34.867
No. that's a bad thing.

409
00:25:34.868 --> 00:25:37.870
Pigeons are a bad thing.

410
00:25:37.871 --> 00:25:40.040
Dead pigeons. Frieda.

411
00:26:03.355 --> 00:26:05.064
Hey. there's no one
here golfing.

412
00:26:05.065 --> 00:26:07.067
They probably ran out of balls.

413
00:26:08.860 --> 00:26:11.612
Ah. come on.
Beer can?

414
00:26:11.613 --> 00:26:12.655
Seriously?

415
00:26:20.872 --> 00:26:23.082
Help. someone!

416
00:26:23.083 --> 00:26:25.751
Help!

417
00:26:25.752 --> 00:26:25.794
Hey. down here!
Help!

418
00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:36.054
Help!

419
00:26:39.057 --> 00:26:41.058
Ah. my shoulder.

420
00:26:42.685 --> 00:26:45.938
Come on. come on.

421
00:26:45.939 --> 00:26:47.815
Pop.

422
00:26:47.816 --> 00:26:48.899
Pop. dammit.

423
00:27:03.957 --> 00:27:05.417
Just breathe.
Breathe.

424
00:27:07.752 --> 00:27:11.088
Hey. I'm down here.

425
00:27:11.089 --> 00:27:12.841
Hey.

426
00:27:16.261 --> 00:27:17.846
Move. Anna.

427
00:27:19.514 --> 00:27:21.098
Move. Anna.

428
00:27:21.099 --> 00:27:22.434
I know you can do it.

429
00:27:24.310 --> 00:27:25.978
You're breathing.

430
00:27:33.737 --> 00:27:35.780
You're conscious.

431
00:27:36.906 --> 00:27:39.950
Move. Anna.
You have to move.

432
00:27:39.951 --> 00:27:41.493
Before you pass out.

433
00:28:07.395 --> 00:28:10.314
- This is too hard.
- You can do it.

434
00:28:10.315 --> 00:28:12.900
You can do it. Anna.

435
00:28:12.901 --> 00:28:15.904
Rock by rock.

436
00:28:23.411 --> 00:28:25.580
I know you can do it.

437
00:30:03.094 --> 00:30:05.679
Sh...!

438
00:30:05.680 --> 00:30:09.058
Hey. uh. I felt bad about
leaving so abruptly.

439
00:30:09.059 --> 00:30:10.934
I just fell off a cliff.

440
00:30:14.022 --> 00:30:16.649
- Did you consider the ER?
- I have a dislocated shoulder.

441
00:30:16.650 --> 00:30:18.984
a concussion and a scrape.

442
00:30:18.985 --> 00:30:22.237
All they'll do is make me wait
and give me sepsis.

443
00:30:22.238 --> 00:30:24.615
It was a tiger trap.
- Literally?

444
00:30:24.616 --> 00:30:26.367
A tarp with leaves
and dirt on it.

445
00:30:26.368 --> 00:30:28.535
so it looked like solid ground.

446
00:30:28.536 --> 00:30:31.080
Someone lured me there
with a false call.

447
00:30:31.081 --> 00:30:32.623
left litter for me.

448
00:30:32.624 --> 00:30:34.666
and then threw a rock
at my head.

449
00:30:34.667 --> 00:30:38.420
- Should I come back?
- Oh. no. I'm good.

450
00:30:38.421 --> 00:30:40.422
The day can only go up
from here.

451
00:30:40.423 --> 00:30:43.258
- Call me anytime.
- You called me!

452
00:30:43.259 --> 00:30:47.179
- And look out for yourself.
- Enjoy your various crimes.

453
00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:49.140
And go to the hospit...

454
00:30:51.434 --> 00:30:53.978
Hello?

455
00:31:08.159 --> 00:31:10.661
Whoa!

456
00:31:10.662 --> 00:31:13.664
Christina from
the Visitor Center.

457
00:31:13.665 --> 00:31:16.291
What are you doing
in my house. Christina?

458
00:31:16.292 --> 00:31:19.253
Frieda told me you fell.

459
00:31:19.254 --> 00:31:22.506
I put a casserole in your oven.

460
00:31:22.507 --> 00:31:25.008
You were in Sheila's cabin.

461
00:31:25.009 --> 00:31:27.720
Your dish stacking
is quite specific.

462
00:31:27.721 --> 00:31:29.346
It's not what you think.

463
00:31:29.347 --> 00:31:30.556
I think this day's
driven me crazy.

464
00:31:30.557 --> 00:31:33.058
and I might kill someone.

465
00:31:33.059 --> 00:31:35.269
- Mommy!
- Hi!

466
00:31:35.270 --> 00:31:39.523
Your mommy and I were
just about to have a nice chat.

467
00:31:39.524 --> 00:31:43.110
Mm-hmm.

468
00:31:43.111 --> 00:31:43.194
Weren't we?

469
00:31:43.361 --> 00:31:50.659
You and Sheila were dating?

470
00:31:50.660 --> 00:31:54.329
It was over.

471
00:31:54.330 --> 00:31:56.623
We kept it quiet.

472
00:31:56.624 --> 00:32:02.504
I'm going through a bad divorce.
custody issues.

473
00:32:02.505 --> 00:32:05.300
It wasn't him.
He's working on an oil rig.

474
00:32:08.178 --> 00:32:13.807
When I heard Sheila died.
I went and tidied her place.

475
00:32:13.808 --> 00:32:17.227
Felt like. uh.

476
00:32:17.228 --> 00:32:19.104
taking care of her
one last time. you know?

477
00:32:19.105 --> 00:32:20.773
Man. I knew
she had a crush on you.

478
00:32:20.774 --> 00:32:22.275
Yeah.

479
00:32:25.362 --> 00:32:26.696
Why'd you guys break up?

480
00:32:29.407 --> 00:32:31.325
- I hate hiking.
I just...

481
00:32:31.326 --> 00:32:33.494
- What?
- Yeah.

482
00:32:33.495 --> 00:32:35.245
Nah. you're not doin' it right.

483
00:32:37.749 --> 00:32:41.044
Can you see
if you can open this?

484
00:32:53.390 --> 00:32:55.432
Is that...

485
00:32:55.433 --> 00:32:59.436
Yeah. Jeremiah D. Paulson.

486
00:32:59.437 --> 00:33:02.065
one of the biggest
landowners in Montana.

487
00:33:04.109 --> 00:33:06.152
She dropped a pin in the map
right here.

488
00:33:08.071 --> 00:33:11.281
Where are you going?

489
00:33:11.282 --> 00:33:13.410
Hunting.

490
00:34:09.841 --> 00:34:13.594
You're okay...

491
00:34:13.595 --> 00:34:16.389
You're okay. you're okay.

492
00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:22.270
Slide me your gun. Anna.

493
00:34:24.939 --> 00:34:28.233
Hi. Harlan.

494
00:34:33.573 --> 00:34:36.409
Kick it over.

495
00:34:37.952 --> 00:34:40.245
That's it.

496
00:34:40.246 --> 00:34:41.789
Jeremiah Paulson's
leading hunting trips

497
00:34:41.790 --> 00:34:44.291
in the park. isn't he?
You're poaching.

498
00:34:44.292 --> 00:34:46.168
Don't say things
you can't prove.

499
00:34:46.169 --> 00:34:47.336
You called him "Jerry D"
like you know him.

500
00:34:47.337 --> 00:34:49.546
You used to hunt in Alaska.

501
00:34:49.547 --> 00:34:51.632
You're a ranger. Harlan.
Why?

502
00:34:51.633 --> 00:34:54.927
'Cause sunsets are golden.
but they ain't money.

503
00:34:54.928 --> 00:34:57.304
Don't you...

504
00:34:57.305 --> 00:34:59.348
I don't wanna have
to kill you. Anna.

505
00:34:59.349 --> 00:35:01.183
Sheila was tracking the cats.

506
00:35:01.184 --> 00:35:03.685
She found out about
the poaching. didn't she?

507
00:35:03.686 --> 00:35:07.189
She told you because
she trusted you.

508
00:35:07.190 --> 00:35:09.692
And you told her
that you'd help her.

509
00:35:09.693 --> 00:35:11.902
Hmm...
I'm curious.

510
00:35:11.903 --> 00:35:14.489
What'd you use to make it
look like a cat bit her?

511
00:35:16.282 --> 00:35:17.991
Screwdriver?

512
00:35:17.992 --> 00:35:20.494
- Just a regular punch.
- Hmm.

513
00:35:20.495 --> 00:35:23.247
So what?
You-You missed hunting?

514
00:35:23.248 --> 00:35:24.832
You missed the army?
You missed killing people?

515
00:35:24.833 --> 00:35:27.459
What was it?
- You can't be like us.

516
00:35:27.460 --> 00:35:30.963
doin' jobs. hoping for the best.

517
00:35:30.964 --> 00:35:32.423
You gotta go where the power is.

518
00:35:32.424 --> 00:35:35.509
- Ah.
And Cory?

519
00:35:35.510 --> 00:35:36.927
Well. I thought maybe
I could pin it on him.

520
00:35:36.928 --> 00:35:40.806
But...
you didn't fall for it.

521
00:35:40.807 --> 00:35:42.349
I hope at least
the pigeon you left me

522
00:35:42.350 --> 00:35:44.268
died a natural death.

523
00:35:44.269 --> 00:35:47.688
- Why do you care so much. Anna?
- Someone has to.

524
00:35:49.983 --> 00:35:53.403
Ahh!

525
00:35:58.033 --> 00:36:01.452
Ahh!

526
00:36:06.958 --> 00:36:09.210
Go find your babies. mama.

527
00:36:13.465 --> 00:36:17.301
Roll over.

528
00:36:19.721 --> 00:36:23.057
Put your hands behind your back.

529
00:36:23.058 --> 00:36:25.809
Oh. ahh!

530
00:36:30.357 --> 00:36:31.482
What. are you just
gonna leave me

531
00:36:31.483 --> 00:36:34.985
out here alone to die. Anna?

532
00:36:34.986 --> 00:36:37.071
Maybe you won't be alone.

533
00:36:37.072 --> 00:36:40.700
Maybe she'll come back.

534
00:36:42.994 --> 00:36:43.203
Here. kitty. kitty!

535
00:37:20.865 --> 00:37:23.659
- Miss Pigeon?
I'm Jeremiah Paulson.

536
00:37:23.660 --> 00:37:25.494
I just heard so much about you.

537
00:37:25.495 --> 00:37:27.871
I just really wanted to
officially meet you.

538
00:37:27.872 --> 00:37:30.290
I'm surprised
I didn't meet you last night.

539
00:37:30.291 --> 00:37:33.752
By the cougar Harlan caught
for you to hunt.

540
00:37:33.753 --> 00:37:37.381
- What a fantastical thought.
- Yeah!

541
00:37:37.382 --> 00:37:39.842
I know you've been poaching
in the park. Jeremiah.

542
00:37:39.843 --> 00:37:41.802
Well. I don't really think

543
00:37:41.803 --> 00:37:43.846
you know
what you're talking about.

544
00:37:43.847 --> 00:37:47.641
But what I do think
is I get what I want.

545
00:37:47.642 --> 00:37:49.893
Which is what. exactly?

546
00:37:49.894 --> 00:37:51.854
Glacier has more resources
than just cats. Ms. Pigeon.

547
00:37:51.855 --> 00:37:53.981
From the big sky to the ground

548
00:37:53.982 --> 00:37:57.109
and everything around.
I want it all.

549
00:37:57.110 --> 00:37:59.653
Hmm.

550
00:37:59.654 --> 00:38:04.950
Well. to be clear.
nothing here is yours.

551
00:38:04.951 --> 00:38:07.995
It belongs to everybody.

552
00:38:07.996 --> 00:38:11.081
And if you even touch one hair
on the park's head.

553
00:38:11.082 --> 00:38:13.208
I'll stop you.
- You better be careful.

554
00:38:13.209 --> 00:38:17.129
'cause some things you say
you're gonna have to do.

555
00:38:17.130 --> 00:38:18.673
What a beautiful day.

556
00:38:24.888 --> 00:38:26.638
What's going on?

557
00:38:26.639 --> 00:38:28.432
I'm taking Piedmont
to animal services.

558
00:38:28.433 --> 00:38:32.062
- Nobody wants him?
- No.

559
00:38:33.438 --> 00:38:36.690
After today.
assuming you want the. uh.

560
00:38:36.691 --> 00:38:40.486
transfer to the Badlands
moved up.

561
00:38:40.487 --> 00:38:43.657
You're leaving. right?

562
00:38:49.454 --> 00:38:53.749
I think I'll stay.

563
00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:55.752
I'll keep it warm for you.
in case I change my mind.

564
00:39:00.757 --> 00:39:03.926
- I'll take 'em.
- Really?

565
00:39:06.763 --> 00:39:10.891
What have I got to lose?

566
00:39:13.478 --> 00:39:15.771
What if we let down
our defenses?

567
00:39:15.772 --> 00:39:17.815
What if we let just one person.

568
00:39:17.816 --> 00:39:22.236
one creature in at a time?

569
00:39:22.237 --> 00:39:25.364
Our lives are interconnected.

570
00:39:37.168 --> 00:39:41.922
Ranger Sheila Drury.
this is your final call.

571
00:39:41.923 --> 00:39:44.217
We'll see you on the other side.

572
00:39:57.439 --> 00:40:00.941
- Hey.
- Hey.

573
00:40:00.942 --> 00:40:06.238
- You okay?
- Uh. I mean...

574
00:40:06.239 --> 00:40:08.241
Fell off a cliff.

575
00:40:09.200 --> 00:40:11.952
Can I... get you anything?

576
00:40:11.953 --> 00:40:14.246
Just wanted to see you.

577
00:40:14.247 --> 00:40:16.957
Look. yesterday would have
been my husband's 40th.

578
00:40:16.958 --> 00:40:18.959
I'm. uh...

579
00:40:18.960 --> 00:40:20.794
I don't know your name.

580
00:40:20.795 --> 00:40:23.297
I don't...
I don't know your birthday.

581
00:40:23.298 --> 00:40:27.384
I-I just.
- It's Jesse.

582
00:40:27.385 --> 00:40:30.387
Maybe one day you'll ask.

583
00:40:30.388 --> 00:40:33.015
Okay.

584
00:40:33.016 --> 00:40:34.184
- Come to the bar.
You know where to find me.

585
00:41:48.591 --> 00:41:52.219
In this life.
nobody really walks alone.

586
00:41:53.930 --> 00:41:55.597
Except the cat.
